Speed: zebkit_max_speed_patterns for Rust crates that ask for optimize.

patches/1007 compiles the code zebkit_max_speed_patterns names at -O2
(optimize_max) in place of default_optimization, through the wrappers of
BUILDCONFIG.gn, which Rust crates do not go through. Some crates ask for
//build/config/compiler:optimize themselves, which is opt-level s when
optimize_for_size: among them those of Skia's PNG encoder (png, fdeflate,
flate2, miniz_oxide), which Chrome builds at opt-level 3. cargo_crate()
now gives a library crate a pattern names optimize_max (opt-level 3) in
place of optimize.

At opt-level s, encoding a 1280 by 800 screenshot took 68 ms, a frame
more than Chrome for every Page.captureScreenshot and page.screenshot
(profiles/slim.gn).

--- a/build/rust/cargo_crate.gni
+++ b/build/rust/cargo_crate.gni
@@ -209,6 +209,18 @@
     assert(_crate_type == "rlib")
     _target_type = "rust_static_library"
     _configs = invoker.library_configs
+
+    # zebkit: a crate zebkit_max_speed_patterns names that asks for
+    # Chromium's optimize config (opt-level s when optimize_for_size) gets
+    # optimize_max (opt-level 3), as patches/1007 does for C++.
+    if (zebkit_max_speed_patterns != [] &&
+        filter_include([ get_label_info(":$target_name", "dir") + "/" ],
+                       zebkit_max_speed_patterns) != [] &&
+        filter_include(_configs, [ "//build/config/compiler:optimize" ]) !=
+        []) {
+      _configs -= [ "//build/config/compiler:optimize" ]
+      _configs += [ "//build/config/compiler:optimize_max" ]
+    }
   }
 
   if (defined(invoker.output_name)) {
